sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Client as Controller Client
    participant SignalR as ASP.NET Core Signaling Hub
    participant Host as Host Daemon / Agent
    participant Coturn as Coturn STUN/TURN Relay

    Client->>SignalR: Request Session Connection (DeviceID or 9-digit Support Code)
    SignalR->>Host: Dispatch Connection Invitation & Auth Challenge
    
    alt Attended Support Mode
        Host->>Host: Display Interactive User Consent Dialog
        Host-->>SignalR: User Grants Full Control
    else Unattended Mode
        Host->>Host: Verify Client Cryptographic Signature & Argon2id Hash
        Host-->>SignalR: Unattended Authorization Confirmed
    end

    Client->>SignalR: Request Ephemeral TURN Credentials
    SignalR-->>Client: Return RFC 5766 HMAC-SHA1 TURN Tokens
    Host->>SignalR: Request Ephemeral TURN Credentials
    SignalR-->>Host: Return RFC 5766 HMAC-SHA1 TURN Tokens

    Client->>SignalR: Send WebRTC SDP Offer (Codecs, Resolutions)
    SignalR->>Host: Forward SDP Offer
    Host->>SignalR: Send WebRTC SDP Answer
    SignalR->>Client: Forward SDP Answer

    par Trickle ICE Candidate Exchange
        Client->>SignalR: Stream Client ICE Candidates (Host, Srflx, Relay)
        SignalR->>Host: Deliver Client Candidates
    and
        Host->>SignalR: Stream Host ICE Candidates (Host, Srflx, Relay)
        SignalR->>Client: Deliver Host Candidates
    end

    Client->>Host: ICE Connectivity Checks (STUN Binding Requests)
    
    alt Direct P2P Success (Same LAN or Full-Cone NAT)
        Client<===>Host: Direct UDP WebRTC Connection (DTLS 1.3 / SRTP)
    else Direct P2P Blocked (Symmetric NAT / Strict Firewall)
        Client<===>Coturn: Relayed DTLS-SRTP Media
        Coturn<===>Host: Relayed DTLS-SRTP Media
    end

    Client<===>Host: E2EE Key Exchange (X25519 ECDH over SCTP opendesk-control)
    Host-->>Client: Stream Encrypted H.264 Video & Opus Audio
    Client-->>Host: Stream Encrypted Synthetic Input & Clipboard Packets
